'''Neel''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Myykian]] [[youngling]] who lived on the isolated planet of [[At Attin]] and was best friends with another child named [[Wim]] during the early [[New Republic Era]].<ref name="Real Adventure" /> Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="SkelCrewDate">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> Wim found an [[Onyx Cinder|old starship]] buried in the [[Forest|woods]] outside [[Unidentified city (At Attin)|their city]]. After the two and two other children named [[KB]] and [[Fern]] investigated the ship, they accidentally activated it and became lost in space. The group of kids then forged an alliance with the ship's [[droid]] [[SM-33]] and a [[Force-sensitive]] man called [[Jod Na Nawood]] to find their way back home and avoid a [[Silvo's pirates|crew of pirates]].<ref name="Official Trailer 22">{{SWYouTube|f19gfOMZTtg|Skeleton Crew &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|date=2024-11-01}}</ref>

==Biography==
===Early life===
[[File:Neel-MP.png|thumb|left|250px|Neel, child of At Attin]]
Neel was born as the first of four children around the beginning of the [[Galactic Civil War]] on [[At Attin]]. However, due to the secluded nature of At Attin, he was unaware of the war and did not even know of the [[Destruction of Alderaan]] until 9 ABY. By 9 ABY he attended [[At Attin Middle School Gamma]] together with his best friend [[Wim]], his crush [[Roona (individual)|Roona]] and the girls [[KB]] and [[Fern]]. Neel took part in some of Wim's play-pretend and transgressive behavior but was more focused on academics (intending to become an analyst like most of his classmates and his parents, unlike Wim who wanted a more aspirational job) and less willing to get in trouble than Wim.

===Battle of At Attin===
The information Neel had gained through his friendship with [[Hayna]] on [[At Achrann]] proved pivotal during the [[Invasion of At Attin|Battle of At Attin]]. Neel had learned that there was a turbolaser atop the school on At Achrann. Given that At Attin and At Achrann were built according to the same layout, Neel assumed that At Attin would also have such a laser in the same location, which proved true. Neel used the laser to disable the cannons of the pirate ship, allowing [[KB]] aboard the ''[[Onyx Cinder]]'' to get past the Barrier to contact [[Kh'ymm]] who in turn contacted the [[New Republic]]. The New Republic subsequently sent a squadron which engaged the pirates in battle, destroying their ship.<ref name="The Real Good Guys">{{SkeletonCrew|The Real Good Guys}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|You must be a very weak clan.''"<br />"''( Neel sighs ) Yeah, you're probably right. ( grunts ) We never have to fight. For anything.''"<br />"''We have always had to fight just to survive. We fight for food. We fight to protect our friends. We are strong.''"<br />"''But fighting is... Fighting is bad. If you just keep raiding each other, do you think it'll even ever end?''"<br />"''Yes.''"<br />"''If it was me, I'd just say I was sorry. No more fighting.|Hayna, and Neel|<ref name="No At Attin" />}}
[[File:Neel2-SWI234.png|thumb|180px|right|Neel was a quiet, yet loyal friend.]]
Neel was a soft-spoken child who took his duties in school seriously. He was also a loyal friend to Wim, offering to help him study for his assessment test or accompanying him on an adventure.<ref name="Real Adventure" /> Neel detested fighting, believing revenge solves nothing and that conflicts should be resolved peacefully. He aspired to grow up to be an [[analyst]], like his mother.<ref name="No At Attin /> Neel made trumpeting snores in his sleep.<ref name="Astro Problem Ep Guide">{{SW|url=series/skeleton-crew/season-1-episode-3-episode-guide|text="Very Interesting, As an Astrogation Problem" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars: Skeleton Crew}}</ref> Similar to [[KB]] in her friendship with [[Fern]], Neel at times had difficulty asserting his own needs in his friendship with Wim, leading to the latter sometimes being unaware or even dismissive of the former's needs. This trait somewhat softened over the course of his adventure aboard the ''Onyx Cinder'' and Wim's experience with KB taught Neel's best friend to be more aware of the needs of others, including Neel.

Neel was shy, including when it came to romance. He had never talked to [[Roona (individual)|Roona]] despite having a crush on her.<ref name="Real Adventure" /> However, his experiences during the trip aboard the ''Onyx Cinder'', especially his time on [[At Achrann]], led him to get a surge in confidence.<ref name="No At Attin" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Neel first appeared in the [[Disney+]] live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]'', with the character's portrayal combining [[Robert Timothy Smith]]'s voice, the work of performance artist [[Kacie Borrowman]], on-set performance in a costume, an animatronic head, and facial motion capture. The character was originally supposed to be sweet and shy but was changed to a more funny personality during filming.<ref name="Adventure Interview">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-jon-watts-christopher-ford-interview|text=With ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'', Jon Watts and Chris Ford are Ready for Their Own Pirate Adventure}}</ref>

The character was first identified in a listing by [[Wikipedia:Germany|German]] retailer [[Wikipedia:Müller (store)|Müller]] revealing the [[LEGO]] set [[w:c:brickipedia:75374 The Onyx Cinder|75374 The ''Onyx Cinder'']].<ref name="SkelCrewReveal">{{WebCite|url=https://www.mueller.de/p/lego-star-wars-75374-skeleton-crew-die-onyx-cinder-IPN3006172|text=LEGO Star Wars 75374 Skeleton Crew Die Onyx Cinder|date=2024-07-29|work=[[Wikipedia:Müller (store)|Müller]]|language=German|archivedate=20240729184548}}</ref> In response to fan debate as to whether Neel was a [[Ortolan]], [[Leland Chee]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] confirmed Neel's species was its own alien race<ref name="Elephantine">{{Instagram|username=holocronkeeper|url=p/C-LNoySvnKy|name=[[Leland Chee]]|date=2024-08-03|quote=Elephantine #starwarsalien|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/G7W9S|archivefile=File:LelandChee-Elephantine-IG.png|archivefile2=File:LelandChee-Elephantine2-IG.png}}</ref> which was later also confirmed by the series' creator [[Christopher Ford]].<ref name="Adventure Interview" /> The species was later identified as Myykian.<ref name="Neel's Species" /><ref name="Insider">{{InsiderCite|234|Neel Nation: Robert Timothy Smith}}</ref>

